{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal-record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or consider an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer, and afterward may consider only certain convictions, with notice and an individualized assessment.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Monetary penalty not to exceed $1,000 (no prior violation in five years), $5,000 (one prior violation in five years) or $10,000 (two or more in seven years).","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not make any oral or written inquiry regarding an applicant's criminal record prior to making a conditional offer.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application-fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether criminal history is reviewed and that the applicant may submit rehabilitation evidence; the director may order the application fee returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Monetary penalty not to exceed $1,000, $5,000 or $10,000 depending on prior violations; the director may require the application fee be returned.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after overturned director order","requirement":"If a housing provider wins an appeal and the director's order is overturned, that decision is grounds to evict the former applicant it was ordered to house, with at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director's order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days' notice prior to the eviction;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

